The witches parade through the streets
Behind them, crawling on all fours is a well dressed man
The man has long hair obscuring his face, and dragging the ground
Around his neck is an iron collar and chain
As the procession works it's way through the festivities, people stop to jeer at the crawling man

At the top of the palace stairs, Alik stands in a shining suit of armor
The parade reaches the palace stairs, and a witch mounts the steps holding the chain
She makes her ascent and the man crawls behind her

"What is this about Hazel?"
Hazel is taken aback
"I am too accompany you, were you-"
"The dog" Alik hissed
"Why is that here?"
"Oh! A gift from your father. He might be of some use to you" Hazel turns to the prostrate man
"Get up, let the lord take a look at you"
The man stands up. 
He is dressed quite presentably, or he would be if there weren't holes worn in the knees of
his pants, he wasn't dusty from head to toe, and he wasn't barefoot
Hazel gathers a handful of his hair, and cuts it off with a knife
The hair springs away to reveal the face of an amenable young man, maybe 18 years of age
The hair in the witches hand bursts into flame, Alik flinches slightly, and the hound nearly cowers
Alik looks the hound over appraisingly before turning to Hazel
"He's mine now?" Alik asks skeptically
Hazel smiles motheringly
"In your care for a while Alik"
The hound says something genuinely kind and cheerful to Alik